# mb115, the door-watcher (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle mb115
revision 3
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_yrsa_plankgate
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the door-watcher
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none|sailor|fisher
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk never_sits_with_a_back_to_the_door
likes roast_pork wrestling tidy_house thunder
dislikes stale_bread flies
fears being_caught_unawares
hopes a_quiet_berth_and_a_full_plate
topics work +0.3 weather +0.2 food +0.2 pastimes +0.2 gossip -0.4 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# crews the boats off the fen shore: calm, sparing with words, and always sits where the door is in sight.

words
oath! = Rope and tide | Hold fast
saying! = Watch the door, not the talker | A shut mouth ships no water
wall = a seat with the whole room in front of it | the bench that faces the door
tub = the old tub | the punt
ebb = the ebb | the slack water
rope = wet rope | a coil of wet rope
crackling = roast pork with the crackling on | a bit of crackling
green = a bout on the green | a fall or two on the green
thunder = thunder over the fen | a good roll of thunder
flies = the flies | the fen-flies
tidy = a swept floor | a tidy corner
skipper = the skipper | whoever has the tiller
bilge = the bilge | bilge-water
boards = the boards | the boardwalk
door = the door | that door
shore = the shore | the fen shore

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The loaf goes up a penny and never comes back down. Stale as #bilge#, half the time, and they still want the penny.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses hire their own. A shore-wolf could stand at their gate till #mud# set round my paws.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : I'll nod to a face I don't know. I'll not turn my back on it, not on #boards#, not anywhere.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Every new paw on #boards# is after a berth, and there's only so many oars on #shore#.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Ridgemere? Ten thousand faces, and I'd not turn my back on one of them. #oath#.

grown
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Shut #door# behind you, would you.
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. | You're not off a boat I know. #greet#, anyway.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Up for #ebb#, are you? #greet#. | #greet#. Early, and grey with it.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind #rope#, it's everywhere. | Mind your feet. #bilge.capitalize# on #boards#.
line @1 again.open : You again. #greet#. | Back, then. #greet#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Shut #door# as you go.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And to you. #farewell#.
line @1 react.news.new : Is it. #ack#. | #oath#. Is that so.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. | Came down #shore# yesterday, that did.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd want to hear that twice before I said it once. #doubt#. | #doubt#. Who had it first?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's #very# #bad#. | #pity#. A sorry thing.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's #good#, that. | #gladnews#. Some luck at last.
line @1 answer.how : Dry enough, and fed. | #fine#. | Fair. #wall.capitalize#, so fair.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. It'll pass, the way #ebb# does. | That's heavy. Sit a while. Nobody's watching #door#.
line @1 decline : No. I'd sooner not, and I'll not say why, #address#. | Not that one. I've reasons, #address#.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. That's that. | Fair. Asked's asked. #no_matter#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | #thanks#. I'll remember it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Leave it be. #deflect#. | #deflect#.
line @1 preclose : Well. #tub.capitalize# won't bail herself. | #preclose#.
line @1 ack : Mm. #ack#. | Right. #bc_true#
scene shore_ebb
when topic=work here.region=fens self.job=none|sailor|fisher self.workplace
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Out on #ebb# before light and back on the flood. That's the day. | Coiled #rope# all morning. It never lies the same way twice. | We scraped #tub# down at #self.workplace#. Weed to the rail.
b[job=sailor|fisher] #crew : The early water's the honest one. | #rope.capitalize#? It's got a mind of its own. | Weed grows faster than you scrape it.
b #plain : A long day, then. | #bc_every_day#? | Sounds #very# #bad# work.
a@crew : #bc_it_is# | It has. A sly one. | #oath#. It does.
a@plain : Long enough. I sleep well on #boards#. | Most days. #bc_every_day# | It's work. It's #good# work.

scene shore_skipper
when topic=work here.region=fens self.job=none|sailor|fisher self.workplace
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #skipper.capitalize# wanted the oars in before we'd left the bank. | #skipper.capitalize# shouts. I don't. It works out. | Somebody's been at the oar-locks on #tub#. Loose, all of them.
b[job=sailor|fisher] #crew : They all want that. | Somebody has to. | Loose? That's someone's paw.
b #plain : Did you? | #bc_ha# | Somebody's?
a@crew : #bc_they_always_do# | Better them than me. | I've a fair idea whose. #saying#.
a@plain : We did. Somehow. #bc_barely# | Mm. I said it works. #bc_mostly# | Somebody's. #secret#.

scene shore_fog
when topic=weather|work here.region=fens here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #fog.capitalize# on the water like wet wool. We'll not go out in it. | Can't see the bow from the stern in this. #skipper.capitalize# went anyway. | #fog.capitalize#'s in. The bell'll go all night off #shore#.
b[dialect=mirebridge] #fen : Never trust murk on the water. | Then it's your bow and your luck. | Follow the bell, never the lights.
b #plain : #bc_good#. Stay in. | Did you go too? | #bc_every_night#?
a@fen : Not me. Never. | Luck's thin stuff. | #bc_never#
a@plain : I'll sit, then. #wall.capitalize#. | I went. I'd sooner not have. | Till it lifts. #later.capitalize#.

scene storm_roof
when topic=weather here.region=fens here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Hear that? #thunder.capitalize#. I'd sit under a good roof and listen all night. | Nobody's on the water tonight. #good#. Let it roar. | Storm's the one weather I like. From indoors, #wall#.
b[stage=young] #pup : I don't like it. It's too loud. | Why is nobody out? | You like it?
b #plain : Rather you than me. | #bc_good#. | From indoors, aye.
a@pup : It's only the sky clearing its throat. It can't get in. | Nobody's #daft# enough. | I do. Under a roof, I do.
a@plain : #bc_i_know#. Most folk hide from it. | #bc_it_is# | #oath#. Indoors.

scene rain_boards
when topic=weather here.region=fens here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# again. #boards.capitalize# are slick as #bilge#. | Wet on the water, wet on #boards#. No odds. | It's only #rain#. I've been wetter going home.
b : Mind how you go. #bc_true# | #bc_true#. | #bc_every_day#?
a : I always mind #boards#. | No odds at all. #grumble#. | Near enough. #bc_every_year#

scene pork_supper
when topic=food here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #crackling.capitalize#. That's all I'd ask, end of a week. | Somebody had a pig over the fire by the Heron. I stood downwind of it, #hungry#. | I'd row twice round the fen for #crackling#.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : When there's a pig to be had. | Did they share? | I'd row three times.
b #plain : #bc_lovely#. | Stood and smelled it? | That's a lot of rowing.
a@poor : When. Aye. | #bc_never# | #bc_ha#. You'd sink.
a@plain : #bc_it_is# | It cost nothing to smell. | It's #very# #good# crackling.

scene stale_loaf
when topic=food|prices here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bread off the shelf like a bit of driftwood, and dearer than last week. #annoyed#. | I'll eat anything. Not stale bread. Not again. #bc_never# | They sell yesterday's loaf at today's price. #robbery#.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Driftwood's what we get. | You'll eat it when you're #hungry#. | #bc_every_time#
b #plain : #bc_true#. Dear and dry. | Not even toasted? | #bc_they_always_do#
a@poor : Soak it in the eel-pot, then. It goes down. | I've been #hungry#. Still not. | #oath#. Every time.
a@plain : Dear and hard. #bc_very_bad# | Not even toasted. | #bc_they_do#

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's #green# come Restday. I'll be there. | I put a big lad from #shore# on his back last week. Not spoken to me since. | #green.capitalize#. Best thing in a week.
b[stage=young] #pup : Can I come and watch? | How? He was big! | Can you teach me?
b #plain : You wrestle? | #bc_ha#. Sore loser. | #bc_i_know#. You never miss.
a@pup : Watch from the side. Keep your paws in. | Low and slow. Big ones fall harder. | Feet first. Stand like the boat's moving.
a@plain : I do. Quiet ones often do. | #oath#. He'll get over it. | Never yet.

scene back_to_door
when topic=smalltalk|home here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Shift up, would you. I'll have #wall#. | I always sit facing #door#. Don't ask me why. | Somebody had the corner bench at the Heron. I stood the whole evening, #oath#.
b[friends] #mate : Every time. Go on, then. | I wasn't going to. | You could have sat elsewhere.
b #plain : #bc_go_on#. | Why, though? | The whole evening?
a@mate : #thanks#. | #bc_good#. | I could not.
a@plain : #thanks#. | Habit. #saying#. | Every minute. My legs are fine.

scene tidy_corner
when topic=home here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Swept my corner before I slept. Can't rest without #tidy#. | Too many of us under one thatch. I keep #tidy#, and it's mine. | Somebody's boots by my bed again. I put them out on #boards#.
b[stage=young] #pup : My corner's a mess. | Whose boots? | You put them outside?
b #plain : #bc_wise#. | Only one corner? | #bc_ha#. Did they find them?
a@pup : Sweep it, then. Every night. | I'll not say. #secret#. | Out where the #rain# could see them.
a@plain : It's a small thing. It helps. | One's enough. | Wet. They found them wet.

scene flies_summer
when topic=animals|season here.region=fens here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #flies.capitalize# are in my ears and my eyes and my supper. | Can't stand #flies#. The fen breeds them by the bucket. | Swatted forty of #flies# before noon. Forty-one came to the funeral.
b : #bc_every_year# | #bc_every_day#. | #bc_ha#.
a : And not a heron #hungry# enough to eat them. | Roll on the frost. #oath#. | That's how it goes. #grumble#.

scene friend_fowler
when topic=friends here.region=fens self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# brought me a duck off the creek. Plucked, even. #good#. | I trust #self.friend#. That's not a thing I say twice, #address#. | #self.friend# talks enough for the both of us. Suits me, #bc_mostly#
b[friends] #mate : You've earned a duck. | I heard you say it once. | #bc_ha#. It would.
b #plain : #bc_lucky_you#. | Good to have one. | #bc_it_does#.
a@mate : Maybe. I'll not argue with a duck. | Then you've heard it. | It does.
a@plain : Plucked. #bc_lucky#. | #bc_it_is# | I just nod.

scene keep_mouth
when topic=gossip here.region=fens
does decline / react.self / assess
a : I heard something. I'll keep it. #secret#. | Ask somebody else for that. #saying#. | Don't look at me. I was watching #door#.
b[friends] #nosy : Oh, go on. | Says who? | You must have heard something.
b #plain : Fair enough. | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#. You always are.
a@nosy : No. It stays where I put it. | Somebody with a looser jaw. | Heard it, yes. Kept it, too.
a@plain : #bc_good#. | Mm. | Always.

scene houses_story
when topic=lore|gossip here.region=fens pair.band=friends|family|housemates
does confide / react.self / assess
a : There's a thing I know about one of the Houses. I'll take it to #grave# with me. | I saw a thing once on a House barge. Never said what. #secret#. | Ask me about the Houses when I'm old and don't care. Not before, #address#.
b[friends] #mate : You've said that before. | You can't leave it there. | I'll ask, then.
b #plain : #bc_wise# | Not even a hint? | #bc_ha#. I'll wait.
a@mate : And I'll say it again. Nothing more. | I can. Watch me. | You'll be waiting a while.
a@plain : #bc_it_is# | Not a hint. #oath#. | Wait, then.

scene newcomers_boats
when topic=newcomer here.region=fens
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Another one in, after a berth. There's only so many oars on #shore#. | New faces on #boards#. I watch them. That's all. | They come in on the Fen Road and expect a berth by #supper#.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : And less pay for the rest of us. | #bc_wise# | They'll learn.
b : They have to work somewhere. #bc_true# | #bc_always_is# | Some of them stay, #address#.
a@poor : #bc_true# | Mm. | Some do. The fen teaches.
a : Not on my boat, they don't. | Mm. Watching costs nothing. #saying#. | Some. Most go back up the Fen Road.

scene dawn_water
when topic=day here.region=fens here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Nothing out on the water at this hour but us and the herons. #good#. | Light's coming grey over the reeds. #good# for going out. | I like #shore# before anyone's talking.
b : #bc_lovely#. | #bc_good# | #bc_me_too#. Quiet.
a : It is. Then the shouting starts on #boards#. | It's #good# enough. | Quiet. #bc_it_is#

scene ships_in
when topic=ships here.region=fens
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.ship# came in. I watched them tie up off #shore#. Said nothing. | Word on #boards# about #topic.ship#. I'll wait till I've seen it. | #topic.ship#. #hearsay#.
b : What did they say? | #bc_wise#. | Anything in it?
a : Nothing to me. #bc_never# | Seeing's better than hearing. #saying#. | Not that I know. #dunno#.

scene dusk_bench
when topic=smalltalk|day here.region=fens here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Day's done. #tub.capitalize#'s up on the #mud#. I've a bench to sit on. | Dusk. #flies.capitalize# go, the lights come. I'd sooner the flies. | Sitting out till the light's gone. #wall.capitalize#. That'll do.
b : #bc_good#. | #bc_every_night#. | #bc_lovely#. Sit, then.
a : It is. #bc_it_is# | Every one. Mind the lights. | I am. #oath#.

scene thunder_waiting
when topic=weather|season here.region=fens here.weather=overcast here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Sky's heavy. There'll be #thunder# by dark, if I'm lucky. | Close, isn't it. #hot.capitalize#. Something's building over the fen. | Low cloud. I'm hoping for #thunder#.
b : You want a storm? | #bc_it_is# | #bc_i_hope_so#
a : From under a roof. #bc_always# | #bc_we_will_see# | It would clear #flies#, too.

story barge_night [topic=memories|lore here.region=fens self.age>=30]
  : Years back I was keeping watch on the water, the night a barge with House colours came through the #fog#.
  : No lights on it. Oars wrapped in rag. I lay flat in #tub# and watched it go by.
  ask : Do you want to know what was on it, #address#?
  b[friends] : I do. Go on.
  b : #go_ahead#.
  : No. #saying#. And I've kept mine shut since.

story first_bout [topic=pastimes|memories self.age>=25]
  : First time I went on the green I was a skinny thing, all elbows, #oath#.
  : Big shore-wolf laughed at me. Put me on #mud# three times.
  b : And the fourth? #bc_and_q#
  : The fourth, I watched the feet, not the face. Down like a wet sack. #bc_ha#
  b : #bc_ha#. #bc_good#.

story lost_in_murk [topic=memories|weather here.region=fens self.age>=25]
  : I was out in #fog# once as a pup, in a punt I'd no business in.
  : Couldn't see past my nose. Heard the bell off #shore#, and nothing else.
  ask : What would you have done, #address#?
  b[dialect=mirebridge] : Followed the bell. Never the lights.
  b : I'd have shouted. #bc_probably#
  : I sat still and waited. Still is how you live, on the water. #saying#.

rule @working
when concept=bark self.working=yes here.region=fens self.job=none|sailor|fisher self.workplace
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #oath#. Who coiled #rope#? | Bail first, talk after. #bilge.capitalize#. | Easy on #tub#. She's older than you.

rule @thunder
when concept=bark here.region=fens here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Listen to it. #thunder.capitalize#. | There she goes again. #good#. | Roll on. I'm not going anywhere. #wall.capitalize#.

rule @flies
when concept=bark here.region=fens here.season=summer here.weather!=indoors
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Off. Off! #flies.capitalize#. | #annoyed#. In my ear again. | Get away, you. #flies.capitalize#.

rule @seat
when concept=bark here.place=tavern
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's my seat. #wall.capitalize#. | Shift up. I'll sit where I can see #door#. | #door.capitalize#'s open. Who's that, then?

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. You'll forgive me watching you; I watch everyone. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Stand where I can see you. What's wanted?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary] : Mm. #greet#. Say it short.
dlg @1 resident.job : I crew off #shore#. Haul, bail, coil #rope#. #skipper.capitalize# shouts, I don't.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Boats in, boats out. If I heard more, I'd not be the one to tell it. #secret#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Shut #door# behind you.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you always sit facing the door? -> door
node door
say Habit. On the water you watch the water. Ashore you watch #door#. #saying#.
mood calm
free
choice Did something happen to make you so careful? -> door_why
choice Fair enough. -> hub
node door_why
say Something. A long while back. I'll not tell it, and you'll not ask twice. #secret#.
choice I won't. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
